{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-18T09:35:08.971Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Implemented the read model** in the `osq-kernel-storage` crate:\n\n- `crates/kernel/storage/src/model/mod.rs` — public `write_read_model(db_path, snapshots)` and `build_read_model(project_root, db_path)`, the three untyped tables exactly as TypeScript's `osq query` names them, one transaction, and typed inserts. Only archived snapshots get rows; the file at `db_path` is removed first.\n- `crates/kernel/storage/src/model/rows.rs` — pure snapshot→row mapping (`archived_on`, `elapsed_seconds` as `(archive−approved+500)/1000`, null `attempts`/`halts`/`cost` without events, cost null when unreported).\n- `crates/kernel/storage/src/model/error.rs` — `ReadModelError` (`Storage`/`Sqlite`/`Io`), needed because task 1's `StorageError` sits outside this task's scope.\n- `crates/kernel/storage/src/lib.rs` — declares `model` and re-exports the two functions.\n- `crates/kernel/storage/tests/read_model.rs` — proves Fixture project rows, Delete and rebuild, and Rebuild over a stale database by reading typed `rusqlite` values, plus edge tests for the stale-path and error-rendering mutants.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `cargo test -p osq-kernel-storage --test read_model` → 5 passed.\n- `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` → passes (fmt, clippy `-D warnings`, workspace tests, `mutation check not run: OSQ_DIFF is not set`).\n- `cargo mutants` over the changed model files → 0 missed (34 caught, 7 unviable); `lib.rs` yields no mutants.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/210-rust-storage-base/.run/results/2.md`."}}
